title: artis
version: v2026.5.15
date-released: 2026-05-15
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.7728326
license: "BSD-3-Clause"
repository-code: 'https://github.com/artis-mcrt/artis'
abstract: >-
 ARTIS is a 3D radiative transfer code for supernovae and kilonovae. It uses the Monte Carlo method with indivisible energy packets (Lucy (2002), A&A, 384, 725-735, doi:10.1051/0004-6361:20011756). Sim (2007), MNRAS, 375, 154-162, doi:10.1111/j.1365-2966.2006.11271.x, and Kromer & Sim (2009), MNRAS, 398, 1809-1826, doi:10.1111/j.1365-2966.2009.15256.x, describe the early versions. The latest version has polarisation and virtual packets (Bulla, Sim & Kromer (2015), MNRAS, 450, 967-981, doi:10.1093/mnras/stv657). It also has non-LTE physics for the nebular phase of Type Ia supernovae (Shingles et al. (2020), MNRAS, 492, 2029-2043, doi:10.1093/mnras/stz3412). It also has alpha, beta, and fission decays with time-dependent thermalisation (Shingles et al. (2023), ApJL, 954, L41, doi:10.3847/2041-8213/acf29a).
